These import examples use deep subpath specifiers (`@objectstack/spec/api/endpoint` and `@objectstack/spec/shared/http`), but the package `exports` currently only exposes top-level subpaths like `./api` and `./kernel`. With an `exports` map present, deep imports will fail for consumers unless those subpaths are explicitly exported. Either change the examples to supported imports (e.g. from `@objectstack/spec/api` / `@objectstack/spec/shared`) or add the corresponding `exports` entries in `packages/spec/package.json`.
```suggestion
import { RateLimitSchema } from '@objectstack/spec/api';

// ✅ v3.0 canonical location
import { RateLimitConfigSchema } from '@objectstack/spec/shared';
```
